<section class="w3-faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="w3-faq-title">
  <div class="w3-faq-inner">
    <header class="w3-faq-heading">
      <p class="w3-faq-kicker"><span aria-hidden="true">06</span> CLEAR ANSWERS</p>
      <h2 id="w3-faq-title">Questions about<br /><em>finding a leak?</em></h2>
      <p>What to know before arranging a leak detection inspection in Houston.</p>
      <a class="w3-faq-contact-link" href="#contact">Still have a question? Prepare an inquiry <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </header>

    <div class="w3-faq-list">
      <details class="w3-faq-item">
        <summary><span>What signs can point to a hidden water leak?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <div class="w3-faq-answer"><div><p>An unexplained rise in water use, a damp or warm patch, peeling paint, a musty smell, or water sounds when fixtures are off can be clues. One sign alone does not confirm a leak, but noting when and where it happens can help guide an inspection.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="w3-faq-item">
        <summary><span>Will an inspection require opening a wall or floor?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <div class="w3-faq-answer"><div><p>Leak detection focuses on narrowing down the likely source with checks suited to the property. Some methods can be performed without opening a surface, though access needs depend on the plumbing and findings. Detection identifies a likely location; any opening or repair is a separate decision.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="w3-faq-item">
        <summary><span>What equipment may be used to locate the leak?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <div class="w3-faq-answer"><div><p>Depending on the suspected line and conditions, an inspection may use acoustic listening equipment, thermal imaging, pressure checks, or other suitable locating methods. The right tools vary by property and the clues present.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="w3-faq-item">
        <summary><span>Does leak detection include the repair?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <div class="w3-faq-answer"><div><p>This page is about leak detection and inspection. Locating a suspected leak and repairing it are different scopes of work; ask the provider what the inspection includes and whether repair is offered separately.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="w3-faq-item">
        <summary><span>How much does leak detection cost?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <div class="w3-faq-answer"><div><p>Cost depends on the type of leak, access, and the checks needed. Review the estimate information on this page and confirm the exact scope and price with a provider before scheduling.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="w3-faq-item">
        <summary><span>Which Houston-area communities are shown as service areas?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
        <div class="w3-faq-answer"><div><p>The guide highlights Houston, Katy, Cypress, Spring, The Woodlands, Pasadena, Pearland, and Sugar Land. Coverage can vary by provider, so confirm availability for your ZIP code.</p></div></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

